(vector (map (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607172210-kotobase-protocol-layer-extension.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607172200-kotoba-resource-protocol-0.2-addendum.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607032500-kotoba-kotobase-clojure-datomic-relationship.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607060100-kotoba-lang-reverse-domain-rename-batch2.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607162135-kotoba-lang-io-libp2p-real-tcp-transport.edn")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607172300-kotobase-query-protocol-extension"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-17"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607172300: kotobase query-protocol extension — kotobase-query bridge + Datomic/PostgreSQL/Cypher/SPARQL surfaces\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n**Scope**: `kotoba-lang` org — 1 new prerequisite bridge repo + 4 new query-protocol repos\n**Depends on**: ADR-2607172210 (protocol-layer-extension decision — the repo-layout/naming discipline this ADR follows), ADR-2607172200 (KRP 0.2 addendum)\n\n## Context\n\nFollowing the storage-protocol extension (webdav/oci+oras/ipfs-pinning/nostr/sftp, ADR-2607172210), the\nowner asked for four more surfaces: `datomic.kotobase.net`, `postgresql.kotobase.net`,\n`cypher.kotobase.net`, `sparql.kotobase.net`. These are a different class of work from the prior five:\nthose were storage/object protocols (get/put bytes by key or path, IStore is already sufficient). These\nfour are **query-language protocols** — each implies translating a query language (Datomic's query\nshape, SQL, openCypher, SPARQL) into results over kotobase's own data.\n\n**Architectural gap found during research**: `kotobase.store`/`kotobase.local` (what all five shipped\nprotocol repos build on) is a flat get/put/list(prefix-scan)/append `IStore` — not wired to\n`kotoba-lang/arrangement` (the 4-covering index; its own README already frames its indices in Datomic's\nown terminology, spo/pso/pos/ocp ≡ EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET, per ADR-2607032500) or `kqe` (the Datalog query\nengine). None of the four new surfaces can do real cross-record queries against `IStore` alone. This is\na real gap, not just a wire-format translation problem, and this ADR addresses it as a named\nprerequisite rather than letting each protocol repo reinvent an ad-hoc materialize+scan layer\n(confirmed with the owner: build the query bridge once, shared).\n\nPer-protocol feasibility research (confirmed with the owner before this ADR):\n\n- **Datomic**: no single open Datomic wire protocol exists to conform to (Client API is HTTP+transit but\n  not an independently-specified standard; the Peer/transactor protocol is proprietary/undocumented).\n  `org-<body>-<spec>` reverse-domain naming would overclaim — same reasoning ADR-2607060100 used to\n  exclude `json`/`dag-cbor`/`openapi`. Decision: a bare-named repo exposing kotobase's own Datalog-shaped\n  query surface, HTTP+edn, **shape-compatible with the Datomic Client API's request/response shape\n  (`:query`/`:args` in, result-set edn out) — explicitly NOT wire-compatible with proprietary Datomic**,\n  stated up front in the README.\n- **PostgreSQL**: a real, versioned, documented binary wire protocol — the biggest lift of this batch (a\n  real binary frontend/backend handshake AND a SQL-to-Datalog translator, not just a storage adapter).\n  `kotoba-lang/sql` exists but is not reusable here (`sql.core` is a DDL/statement-*generation* DSL, no\n  parsing or execution). Owner confirmed scope: aim for a small real SQL subset (single-table\n  `SELECT ... FROM <collection> WHERE <equality>`, no joins) alongside the wire handshake, not a\n  handshake-only stub — understood as the largest, riskiest item in this ADR.\n- **Cypher**: no existing kotoba-lang graph-query repo. openCypher is a real, citable open spec\n  (openCypher.org) — `org-opencypher-cypher` naming is defensible. HTTP transaction-endpoint shape\n  (Neo4j's HTTP Cypher API — JSON request/response) chosen over Bolt (binary, stateful, much bigger, no\n  precedent in this workspace) for v0.1 — fits the established `.cljc` HTTP-handler pattern directly.\n- **SPARQL**: most tractable by far — `kotoba-lang/sparql` already exists as a substantial EDN-first\n  algebra (BGP triple-pattern matching, join, filter, union, optional, project, distinct, order-by,\n  slice all already implemented) over `rdf.core`-shaped quads; its `eval-node` takes an in-memory quad\n  collection, not a store. The new protocol-surface repo just needs to materialize kotobase-query bridge\n  output as quads and wrap the (genuinely simple: HTTP GET/POST + `query` param, JSON/XML/CSV results)\n  SPARQL 1.1 Protocol around it. Naming collision: the bare name `sparql` is already taken by the algebra\n  library itself, so the new protocol-surface repo is `org-w3-sparql-protocol` (SPARQL 1.1 Protocol is a\n  W3C spec, matches this org's existing `org-w3-*` convention), depending on `kotoba-lang/sparql`.\n\nThis ADR does not add new KRP identity mappings (ADR-2607172200) — these four are query *interfaces*\nover data other surfaces already give Name/Content/Location identities to via KRP; a query result set is\nnot itself a new addressable resource kind.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Repo layout\n\n| Item | Name | Depends on | Naming rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Query bridge (prerequisite) | `kotoba-lang/kotobase-query` | `kotobase.store`, `kotoba-lang/arrangement`, `kotoba-lang/kqe` | Bare — internal cross-cutting library, matches `kotobase-protocols`/`kotobase-messenger` naming |\n| Datomic-shape surface | `kotoba-lang/datomic-client-shim` | `kotobase-query` | Bare, explicit \"shape-compatible not wire-compatible\" — no open spec to cite |\n| PostgreSQL wire | `kotoba-lang/org-postgresql-wire` | `kotobase-query` | PostgreSQL wire protocol is real, documented, versioned — open spec |\n| openCypher | `kotoba-lang/org-opencypher-cypher` | `kotobase-query` | openCypher.org is a real, citable open spec |\n| SPARQL 1.1 Protocol | `kotoba-lang/org-w3-sparql-protocol` | `kotoba-lang/sparql` (existing algebra), `kotobase-query` | W3C spec; `sparql` bare name already taken by the algebra library |\n\n### `kotobase-query` bridge — v0.1 scope\n\nGiven one or more `kotobase.store` collections, materialize their documents as datoms/quads\n(`[e a v]`-shaped, consistent with `kotoba-lang/kotobase`'s canonical datom model) and execute queries\nvia `kqe`. v0.1: linear materialization (list + transform, no incremental indexing) is an accepted,\nexplicitly-documented limitation — real indexing via `arrangement`'s 4-covering index is a natural\nfollow-up once there's real query-volume evidence, not a v0.1 requirement. This bridge has no wire\nprotocol of its own; it's a library the four consumer repos depend on.\n\n### Per-protocol v0.1 scope\n\n- **`datomic-client-shim`**: HTTP+edn, `{:query <edn-datalog> :args [...]}` in, `#{[...]}`-shaped result\n  sets out — shape modeled on the Datomic Client API's `d/q` call, not any wire-level compatibility.\n  README states the non-wire-compatibility explicitly and prominently, first paragraph.\n- **`org-postgresql-wire`**: real startup handshake + simple-query subprotocol (binary, `.cljs`-only\n  transport per the `kotoba-lang/dtn`/`org-ietf-sftp` split-core-from-transport precedent) + a small real\n  SQL subset: single-table `SELECT <cols> FROM <collection> WHERE <col> = <literal>`, no joins, no\n  aggregates, no subqueries for v0.1 — document this scope boundary as explicitly as `s3.cljc` documents\n  its own carve-outs, do not imply broader SQL support than this.\n- **`org-opencypher-cypher`**: HTTP transaction endpoint (`POST /db/data/transaction/commit`-shaped),\n  JSON statements in, JSON results out. v0.1: `MATCH`+`WHERE`(equality)+`RETURN` only, no `CREATE`/\n  `MERGE`/variable-length paths/aggregation — same explicit carve-out discipline.\n  no `CREATE`/`MERGE`/variable-length paths/aggregation for v0.1.\n- **`org-w3-sparql-protocol`**: SPARQL 1.1 Protocol (`GET`/`POST` + `query` param, `Accept`-negotiated\n  JSON/XML/CSV results) wrapping `kotoba-lang/sparql`'s existing algebra as-is — the query language\n  subset supported is whatever `kotoba-lang/sparql` already supports (BGP/join/filter/union/optional/\n  project/distinct/order-by/slice), not re-scoped down for this ADR.\n\n## Rejected\n\n- **Reverse-domain naming for `datomic-client-shim`** — no open, independently-specified Datomic wire\n  protocol exists to cite; would overclaim, same reasoning as `json`/`dag-cbor`/`openapi`'s exclusion in\n  ADR-2607060100.\n- **Bolt protocol for Cypher v0.1** — binary, stateful, no precedent in this workspace, much bigger lift\n  than the HTTP transaction-endpoint shape for equivalent v0.1 value; left as a possible future addition,\n  not blocking this ADR.\n- **Per-protocol ad-hoc query/materialization layers** — considered (faster individual starts), rejected\n  for the same reason ADR-2607171700 rejected per-surface repos for the original four storage protocols:\n  shared underlying concern, avoid four duplicated, under-tested implementations of the same\n  IStore-to-queryable-data bridge.\n- **PostgreSQL handshake-only v0.1** — considered as the lower-risk option; owner confirmed the small\n  real-SQL-subset scope instead, accepting the larger lift.\n\n## 現在地の訂正 — bridge/q は共有入口ではない（2026-08-03、ADR-2608039970）\n\n本 ADR は `kotobase-query` bridge を「query surface が共有する経路」として起票し、実際にその形で\n6 surface（本 ADR の 4 + ADR-2607172500 の GraphQL/Gremlin）が landed した。**このうち「Datalog を\n共有 IR にする」部分は撤回する。**\n\n実装が先に答えを出していた: `org-w3-sparql-protocol` は `materialize` だけを使い `bridge/q` を呼ばない\n（自前の SPARQL algebra があるので Datalog に翻訳して戻す意味がない、と同 repo の README が明記）。\n**共有して価値があったのは datom 面（`materialize`）であって Datalog（`q`）ではなかった。**\nADR-2608039970 がこれを正本とし、bridge の公開契約を `materialize` + access path\n（`entity-id` / `entity-attrs` / `by-predicate` / `by-predicate-value` / `refs-to` / `datoms`）に変更した\n（kotoba-lang/kotobase-query#6・#7）。\n\n- `q` / `query` は削除しない。Datalog 形の caller（`datomic-client-shim`）には引き続き正しい。撤回するのは\n  「他 surface が経由すべき入口」という位置づけだけ。\n- **materialize-only 経路は例外ではなく正規経路**。org-w3-sparql-protocol#6 で同 repo の README/docstring を\n  その通りに訂正済み。同 PR で `(:spo db)` の直接 walk を `bridge/datoms` に置き換えた —— access path を\n  公開した最初の版に全面 scan が無く、唯一それを必要とする surface が raw index read に落ちていた。\n- 逆に datom 面を迂回して surface ごとに独自の物理表現を持つことは引き続き禁止。**共有するのは面であって\n  言語ではない。**\n\n## Verification\n\nSame bar as ADR-2607172210: `nbb bin/run_tests.cljs` green in each new repo (including\n`kotobase-query`'s own test suite before any consumer depends on it), `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs\n--check` clean, manual smoke per protocol.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607172210 (kotobase protocol-layer extension — the repo-layout/naming discipline this ADR follows)\n- ADR-2607172200 (KRP 0.2 addendum)\n- ADR-2607032500 (kotoba : kotobase = Clojure : Datomic — the terminology precedent `arrangement`'s\n  spo/pso/pos/ocp ≡ EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET framing already established)\n- ADR-2607060100 (reverse-domain rename batch 2 — the don't-overclaim discipline this ADR's Datomic\n  naming decision follows)\n- ADR-2607161817, ADR-2607162135 (real TCP transport precedent — the core/transport split\n  `org-postgresql-wire` follows)\n"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607172300: kotobase query-protocol extension -- kotobase-query bridge + Datomic/PostgreSQL/Cypher/SPARQL surfaces"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))